====================================================================================================
CHECKS: 6/6 passed
VERDICT (against the declared criteria):
  * The dS_2 induced current is computed directly and matches the published closed form (V1-V4).
  * The current does carry e^2: sigma H = e^2/H^2 * g(mu).  But g depends steeply on the mass, so a tie on the conductivity
    fixes only the combination (e^2/H^2) g(mu), one equation for two unknowns.  No tie fixes the coupling (V5).
  * For a heavy charged field the response is Boltzmann-suppressed, g ~ 4 mu e^{-2 pi mu}; at the electron mass over H0
    the required coupling is exponentially large in 10^39.  No O(1) horizon-conductivity tie can hold for a known charged particle (V6).
  * This is a 2D toy: e has mass dimension there, so e^2/H^2 is not the 4D alpha.  dS_4, fermions, and charge renormalization untested.
  * kappa = 1/2 stays FITTED.  The SM-mass wall is unchanged.
